From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Publish the DP edge before rendering, not after

DKR crashes in __scHandleRDP with sc->curRDPTask null. Twelve hypotheses about
ordering were eliminated one by one -- duplicate edges, SP/DP races, queue
saturation, wrong target task -- and every one was wrong, because the defect is
not an ordering defect at all.

DKR's scheduler carries a watchdog that stock libultra does not have. In
__scHandleRetrace (libultra/src/sc/sched.c):

    if (sc->curRDPTask) gCurRDPTaskCounter++;

    if ((gCurRDPTaskCounter > 10) && (sc->curRDPTask)) {
        set_curRDPTask_NULL = TRUE;
        osDpSetStatus(... DPC_CLR_PIPE_CTR | DPC_CLR_CMD_CTR);
    }
    ...
    if (set_curRDPTask_NULL) sc->curRDPTask = NULL;

Past ten retraces with an outstanding RDP task, Rare's code declares the RDP
hung: it nulls curRDPTask and resets the DP registers, but it does NOT clear
OS_SC_NEEDS_RDP on the task. A DP edge arriving after that walks into
__scHandleRDP, reads curRDPTask == 0 and dereferences null.

That is exactly the state the probe captured at the instant of reception:

    msg=668 curRSP=0x00000000 curRDP=0x00000000 <== NUL
    visee=0x80125FB0 state=0x00000001 flags=0x00000023

curRDPTask null while the targeted task still carries NEEDS_RDP (state = 1).
Only two paths null curRDPTask, and __scHandleRDP clears NEEDS_RDP when it does.
The watchdog is the only path that leaves this combination behind.

The threshold is counted in RETRACES PROCESSED, not in milliseconds:
gCurRDPTaskCounter is reset in __scExec when a task starts and incremented once
per __scHandleRetrace. Publishing the DP edge after send_dl let a whole render
worth of retraces land in between.

The first draft of this patch claimed a software Glide frame blows the 167 ms
that eleven retraces are worth at 60 Hz. The measurement it shipped with refutes
that outright -- worst case 60 ms over more than a thousand frames, zero
overruns. The hypothesis was plausible, it explained the symptom, and the fix it
inspired works; three reasons not to check it, and it was wrong anyway. The
measurement is kept because it watches the worst case, not because it validates
anything.

What the run does show: 3238 VIDEO messages against 567 RDP_DONE, about six
retraces per display list -- comfortably under eleven on average and not under it
in the tail. One excursion is all it takes, which is why the crash struck once,
at display list 344 of a run that was otherwise progressing.

Publishing the edge before rendering is safe for exactly the reason the SP edge
already is: the queued task owns an immutable RDRAM snapshot, so the renderer
never reads memory the game may recycle, and presenting to the screen is the
port's business rather than the game's.

Measured on the machine, same ROM, same build otherwise:

    before   display lists 344, then EXCEPTION in __scHandleRDP
    after    display lists 1135 and climbing, 7020 presents, 0 null receptions

diff --git a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
--- a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
@@ -268,6 +268,13 @@
 //
 // La trace s'arrete d'elle-meme apres quelques centaines de lignes : la machine
 // cible ecrit sur une disquette emulee.
+// Definie par le jeu (game_main.cpp) : vide le journal ET met a jour l'entree de
+// repertoire, faute de quoi un programme fige laisse un fichier de zero octet.
+// Declaree faible pour que les binaires d'epreuve, qui lient ultramodern sans le
+// jeu, se lient quand meme.
+extern "C" void dkr_diag_commit(void) __attribute__((weak));
+static void diag_commit() { if (dkr_diag_commit) { dkr_diag_commit(); } }
+
 static std::atomic<unsigned> g_trace_submits{0};
 static std::atomic<unsigned> g_trace_sp{0};
 static std::atomic<unsigned> g_trace_dp{0};
@@ -284,6 +291,44 @@
                  g_trace_dp.load());
 }
 
+// Combien de temps dure reellement un rendu de liste d'affichage ?
+//
+// C'est la mesure qui a corrige le diagnostic plutot que de le confirmer.
+//
+// L'hypothese etait qu'un rendu logiciel Glide depasse les 167 ms que valent
+// onze retraces a 60 Hz, et fait donc ceder le chien de garde de DKR. Mesure :
+// **pire cas 60 ms sur plus de mille images, zero depassement**. L'hypothese est
+// fausse, et sans ce releve elle serait passee pour etablie -- elle etait
+// plausible, elle expliquait le symptome, et le correctif qu'elle a inspire
+// fonctionne. Trois raisons de ne pas la verifier, et elle est fausse quand meme.
+//
+// Ce que le retard coute n'est pas du temps mais des **retraces traites entre
+// temps** : gCurRDPTaskCounter est remis a zero par __scExec au demarrage d'une
+// tache, puis incremente une fois par __scHandleRetrace. On garde la mesure
+// parce qu'elle continue de surveiller le pire cas, pas parce qu'elle valide
+// quoi que ce soit.
+static std::atomic<unsigned> g_dl_pire_ms{0};
+static std::atomic<unsigned> g_dl_hors_budget{0};
+static std::atomic<unsigned> g_dl_total{0};
+static void trace_dl_duration(std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::time_point debut,
+                              std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::time_point fin) {
+    const unsigned ms = static_cast<unsigned>(
+        std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(fin - debut).count());
+    const unsigned n = g_dl_total.fetch_add(1) + 1;
+    unsigned pire = g_dl_pire_ms.load();
+    while (ms > pire && !g_dl_pire_ms.compare_exchange_weak(pire, ms)) {}
+    // 167 ms = onze retraces a 60 Hz, le seuil exact du chien de garde.
+    if (ms > 167u) { g_dl_hors_budget.fetch_add(1); }
+    if (!trace_sp_enabled()) { return; }
+    if (n % 60u != 0u) { return; }
+    std::fprintf(stderr, "[trace][dl] rendus=%u pire=%u ms hors-budget(>167ms)=%u\n",
+                 n, g_dl_pire_ms.load(), g_dl_hors_budget.load());
+    // Forcer le journal sur le disque. Sans cela, un blocage laisse un fichier
+    // de zero octet quoi qu'on ait ecrit, et l'on ne peut pas distinguer
+    // « le programme s'est arrete tot » de « le programme tourne encore ».
+    diag_commit();
+}
+
 void sp_complete() {
     g_trace_sp.fetch_add(1);
     trace_sp("sp", 0);
@@ -416,11 +461,40 @@
                 PTR(u64) displaylist = task_action->task.t.data_ptr;
                 ultramodern::extensions::on_displaylist_submitted(displaylist);
 
